README for the Web Application

Overview

This web application is designed to scrape GitHub repositories based on tags, review selected repositories, clone them, and perform a security analysis using bluescrub.py. The results of the analysis are presented in a detailed HTML report.

Features

	•	Scrape Repositories: Search for GitHub repositories based on tags and display the results.
	•	Review Selected Repositories: Select repositories from the search results to review and save detailed information.
	•	Clone Repositories: Clone selected repositories to the local machine.
	•	Security Analysis: Run bluescrub.py to perform a security analysis on the cloned repositories and generate a detailed HTML report.
	•	View Analysis Results: View the analysis results directly in the application.
Routes

	•	GET /: Render the home page.
	•	POST /scrape: Scrape GitHub repositories based on tags.
	•	POST /review: Review the selected repositories.
	•	POST /save_selected: Save the detailed information of the selected repositories to a JSON file.
	•	POST /scan_code: Run the security analysis on the selected repository.
	•	POST /clone_repository: Clone the selected repository.
	•	GET /view_analysis/<repo_name>/<filename>: View the detailed analysis results.

Example Usage

	1.	Scrape GitHub Repositories:
	•	Go to the home page and enter tags to search for repositories.
	•	Click the “Scrape” button to display the search results.
	2.	Review and Save Repositories:
	•	Select the repositories you want to review and click “Review Selected”.
	•	On the review page, you can save the detailed information by providing a filename.
	3.	Clone and Scan Repositories:
	•	Click the “Clone Repository” button to clone the selected repository.
	•	Click the “Scan Code” button to run the security analysis on the cloned repository.
	4.	View Analysis Results:
	•	After the scan is complete, view the detailed analysis results directly in the application.

Dependencies

	•	Flask
	•	gitpython
	•	matplotlib
	•	plotly
	•	bandit
	•	pylint
	•	safety
	•	werkzeug

Ensure all dependencies are installed before running the application. You can install them using pip:
pip install flask gitpython matplotlib plotly bandit pylint safety werkzeug

Code Overview

	•	app.py: Main application file containing routes and logic for scraping, reviewing, cloning, and scanning repositories.
	•	bluescrub.py: Script for performing a security analysis on the cloned repositories and generating HTML reports.
	•	templates/: Directory containing HTML templates for rendering different pages.
	•	static/: Directory containing static files such as CSS and JavaScript.

Notes

	•	The application uses Flask for the web interface.
	•	The security analysis is performed by bluescrub.py, which generates detailed HTML reports of the findings.
	•	The application allows users to interactively select, clone, and scan GitHub repositories for security analysis.

This README provides an overview, setup instructions, route descriptions, and example usage for the web application, helping users understand its purpose, features, and how to run it effectively.